[[Open This|Oxide CLI]]

---

Oxide CLI always requires:

an auth profile
a host (control plane URL)
a token/session

Without oxide auth login, it refuses to even send requests.

```
$installDir = "C:\Tools\oxide"
$tempZip = "$env:TEMP\oxide.zip"

# Get latest release
$release = Invoke-RestMethod "https://api.github.com/repos/oxidecomputer/cli/releases/latest"

# Find Windows x64 asset
$asset = $release.assets | Where-Object {
    $_.name -match "windows" -and $_.name -match "x86_64.*\.zip$"
} | Select-Object -First 1

if (-not $asset) {
    Write-Error "Could not find a Windows CLI release."
    exit 1
}

# Download
Invoke-WebRequest $asset.browser_download_url -OutFile $tempZip

# Install
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $installDir | Out-Null
Expand-Archive -Path $tempZip -DestinationPath $installDir -Force

# Add to PATH if needed
$machinePath = [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable("Path", "Machine")

if ($machinePath -notlike "*$installDir*") {
    [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(
        "Path",
        "$machinePath;$installDir",
        "Machine"
    )
}

# Update current session
$env:Path += ";$installDir"

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "Oxide CLI installed to $installDir"
Write-Host ""
Write-Host "Open a NEW PowerShell window and run:"
Write-Host "oxide --version"
```

